+# Feature Specification: Cancel Booking
+
+**Feature Directory**: `specs/005-cancel-booking`
+**Input**: `cancel(bookingId, at)` on the rental service cancels the booking at time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`, the amount given back to the customer. A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment; a booking can only be cancelled once.
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+### User Story 1 - Customer cancels a booking (P1)
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. Cancelling an existing booking returns `{ bookingId, refund }` with the refund in euro cents.
+2. After cancelling, the item is free again for the booked period (`availability`, `book`).
+3. Cancelling the same booking a second time is rejected.
+4. Cancelling an unknown booking id is rejected.
+
+### Edge Cases
+- `at` must be an ISO-8601 UTC instant; anything else is rejected.
+- A rejected cancellation (second cancel, unknown id, invalid `at`) leaves bookings unchanged.
+- `at` after the booking's start (rental under way or over): refund amount is covered by the open question below.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `cancel(bookingId, at)` returns `{ bookingId, refund }`; `refund` is an integer number of euro cents, never more than the booking total.
+- **FR-002**: A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment.
+- **FR-003**: A booking can be cancelled only once; unknown ids throw.
+- **FR-004**: The refund depends on `at` relative to the booking. [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: what is the refund rule? (e.g. full refund until some notice before start, partial later, none after start)]
